error: `UnixStream.connect` holds the thread until it is done, and an async function does not hold its thread
  the tasks of async functions share a few threads: one that holds its thread keeps the others from running
  --> error_net_unix_connect_blocking.sg:2:31
 2 |     var conn = try UnixStream.connect(path)
   |                               ^^^^^^^
  hint: `await UnixStream.connectAsync(path)` does the same work without holding the thread
